Re:Zero − Starting Life in Another World

Arc 10: The Land of the Lion King

Chapter 10.38: “Wait”


---

—A complete change in the circumstances surrounding Kugelschreiber Castle.

Hearing this news from Tīga, Subaru and the others couldn't help but hold their breath.

The castle had crossed through space—which meant, in other words, that it had escaped from its hidden subspace and returned to the surface world for the first time in several hundred years.

However, that was—

“Looks like even you weren't expecting this.”

“—. Well, who knows? Maybe it's all part of our plan to make you think that? Trusting too much in what you see with your own eyes is one of your bad habits, my friend. I've been telling you that for years, haven't I?”

“Lord Subaru, the wind of falsehood…”

“Shhh! Miss Crusch, shhh! We're in the middle of an advanced battle of wits!”

“We're not, we're not. I'm not going to fall for that, obviously. …Though, honestly, being told that I've forgotten something does make my heart skip a beat a little.”

Having gauged Subaru and the others' reactions, Tīga glanced toward Subaru's side, where Melty stood, still watching him.

Melty's gaze as she stared at Tīga was laden with expectation and warmth, carrying a significance that was difficult to ignore. The fact that she'd called his name made it undeniable that there was some kind of relationship between them.

“And it seems you're in the same boat, but… Black Dog, what about your history with that little spirit?”

“I don't remember a single thing, not one tiny little bit! It's the fault of that tiny spirit I don't know! Sorry, my bad, I'm so sorry!”

“…Ah, is that so? Don't worry.”

Like Melty, Black Dog had some complicated circumstances of his own. Apparently, he also had some sort of unusual relationship with the squirrel-like spirit perched on Tīga's shoulder, glaring at them.

Black Dog was acting like this, but based on the experience Subaru had accumulated over the past two months, he judged that the spirit probably wasn't lying.

Frankly, the sheer volume of information being crammed into his head was enough to make him dizzy. But now that Belalis, who had been the cause of so much of that mental overload, had fallen silent, Subaru couldn't use that as an excuse to stop thinking.

—At present, their side consisted of Subaru, Ferris, and Melty, all of whom were half-dead, aside from a healthy Black Dog and a relatively healthy Crusch. Even the first two weren't anywhere near their best, given their injuries and exhaustion. They couldn't afford to do anything reckless.

Still, they did have a glimmer of hope.

And to bring that possibility to fruition—

“Now then, we've got five people on our side, while you've only got two, even counting the little spirit on your shoulder. In terms of numbers, we're more than twice as strong, so we're overwhelmingly advantaged. If you're going to surrender, now's your chance!”

“…Am I hearing things? That guy is saying all that to us based purely on numbers, completely ignoring how beat-up his own side is.”

“You heard him right, Pūka. That's just how my friend is. Though, I have to admit, I'm surprised he's completely disregarding how exhausted everyone is.”

“You have more seriously injured people on your side. That's another advantage for us.”

“With a hole in your back, you say that so confidently that I might actually believe you.”

Tīga shrugged as though he had absolutely no intention of believing Subaru. Apparently, he had no talent for acting whatsoever.

For now, Subaru had gained two things: the squirrel-like spirit's name was Pūka, and their opponents were willing to humor them by continuing the conversation.

Nevertheless, this was little more than an extension of casual conversation, hardly something that could be called negotiations. Crusch and Black Dog, who naturally sensed that a fight was inevitable, gradually grew more eager for battle—

“—The hell are you doing, standing around chatting so leisurely?! Get them! Go on, get them! Finish them off, Executor! That's what you're here for, isn't it?!”

However, the one who had grown impatient with the situation and raised his voice even more than Subaru's group was Reborn.

Using his tailor shears to support himself, Reborn had lost his eyesight to Crusch's sword strike and could no longer use the power of Silence, which depended on his vision.

Even so, relying on his sense of presence, he shouted at Tīga, insisting that he fulfill his duty by which he'd come rushing here.

Hearing his plea, Subaru licked his dry lips, thinking that the man was saying something completely unnecessary.

“…Honestly, the worst-case scenario would be if they just attacked without warning.”

Even if the restrictions imposed by Silence and Ring Finger were gone, allowing Subaru's mouth and mind to work as they normally did, that wouldn't be enough to overcome the decisive gap in strength between them.

He could support the others in battle with the unfair combination of Cor Leonis and Blue, but there was no guarantee how long he could maintain it.

That was why the most troublesome thing Tīga could do right now was to overpower them through sheer force—

“Let's hurry up and take these guys—”

“—Torneru, you can hear me, right? Use Detour at full power. We're getting out of here.”

“Wha—?!”

But Tīga's next words betrayed both Subaru's fears and Reborn's demands.

Calling out by name to the third Beloved Child, who wasn't present, Tīga spun around on the spot and closed the distance to Reborn, whose bloodied face was turned toward him.

Then, with the pommel of his drawn curved sword, he delivered a powerful blow to the back of the motionless Reborn's neck.

“Guh—”

“I told you, time's up. Besides, you're the ones at fault for getting ahead of yourselves without waiting for instructions.”

The diminutive figure let out a brief groan and collapsed. Tīga casually hoisted him over his shoulder, then turned to the stunned Subaru and the others.

“As you heard, we're retreating with our spoiled brats. That's all for today.”

“Whoa, whoa, whoa! That's a pretty damn selfish opinion, isn't it?! You suddenly barge in here, throw out a bunch of riddles, and then just walk away?! Leave your lives and your answers behind!”

“W-What a vulgar and barbaric way of speaking…! I simply can't believe that someone like that is my contractor! Have I been deceived?!”

“How the hell should I know, you idiot?! Go burn yourself out while carrying your baggage! BURNING!”

With that, Black Dog loudly delivered the final word in their exchange and unleashed a raging inferno from his outstretched palm.

The green flames spread sideways like the breath of a Dragon, cutting off every avenue of escape for Tīga, who had the indignant spirit perched on his shoulder.

Faced with this completely unexpected act of aggression, Subaru almost let out a scream.

“B—!”

But a voice even louder than his came from Melty beside him.

It wasn't a scream, however.

“Don't! Fire won't work on Pūka!”

“Huh?!”

Black Dog responded with a puzzled shout at her confident declaration.

The truth of her words was proven when the green flames reached Tīga and the others—and were devoured head-on.

At the center of the surging green inferno, the section directly in front of Tīga and his companions was neatly bitten away and disappeared.

The one responsible was Pūka, who licked her lips.

The adorable-looking spirit lightly wiped her mouth with a forepaw and said,

“That girl seems to understand things pretty well. —That I'm a Great Fire Spirit.”

“If you knew that, then SAY SO! Are you trying to show off how evil you are here?! You've certainly put a lot of effort into your self-promotion!”

“Black Dog attacked out of nowhere! More importantly—”

Melty retorted to Black Dog's unjust complaint, then turned her gaze toward Tīga beyond the divided flames.

As though responding to her signal, Tīga leaped lightly backward while carrying Reborn. Reaching out with one arm, he scooped up the fallen Belalis as well.

“Still alive, are you? Scatter Ring Finger. No need to hold back. —It won't work on me anyway.”

“…Oh? Does that mean… you trust me and… love me? I… feel the same way…!”

Just how tenacious was she?

In response to Tīga's words, Belalis once again answered with her own expression of affection, completely undeterred.

Then came a sweet fragrance that heightened emotions and drove people out of their minds.

Belalis activated Ring Finger once more, spreading the substance that caused emotions to erupt uncontrollably through the air.

“Ferris! I'm gonna be in trouble, so please deal with this! Yahoo!”

“—! You already are! Don't move, don't thrash around! I can't treat you like this!”

Subaru activated their combination strategy: using Cor Leonis to take on the mental abnormalities affecting all his companions, then having Ferris treat him.

Somehow, they managed to hold on.

But even as they dealt with the effects, Tīga, carrying Belalis in a fireman's carry, was making his escape from the battlefield with the two defeated Beloved Children in his possession.

Crusch and Black Dog each moved to stop him—

“I won't let you interfere!”

“—!”

Pūka puffed out her cheeks and roared, spitting back the flames she'd just swallowed from Black Dog.

The green inferno assailed the two who were pursuing Tīga. Crusch severed it with an upward slash and stepped through the curtain of flames—

Straight into Black Dog.

“Kyah?!” “Whoa?!”

Their startled cries overlapped as the two fell over from the unexpected collision.

It was a repeat of the earlier friendly fire caused by Ring Finger—except it wasn't.

“—WHY?! Where'd Tīga go?!”

Beyond the fallen Crusch and Black Dog, Subaru had lost sight of Tīga as well.

It had happened immediately after Pūka's flames blocked his view for a moment, making Tīga and the others disappear from sight.

Subaru doubted his own eyes, unable to understand how he'd lost track of someone who had been right there.

But he wasn't the only one who'd lost sight of Tīga.

Ferris, who was leaning against Subaru despite having lost his arms, was also looking around in confusion, his eyes darting back and forth.

“Huh? Huh?”

Subaru could feel Ferris's healing power more closely than ever.

In other words, this wasn't the effect of Belalis's Ring Finger—

“—Detour?! It doesn't just make people get lost?!”

Detour, which had caused the group to become separated inside the castle and subsequently made it difficult for them to reunite, was still being used by a caster who had yet to reveal themselves.

If it could interfere not only with one's sense of direction but also with one's cognitive abilities, then Tīga had made himself disappear by causing Subaru's gaze and awareness to take a detour away from him.

And just like that, Tīga would escape, running along the outskirts of their consciousness, beyond their ability to do anything about it—

“Wait!”

In that instant, Melty raised her slender voice and stood in his way, gripping her shooting staff.

Subaru caught a faint glimpse of Melty at the edge of his vision. Forcing his head to turn toward her to resist Detour, he saw her standing before the door leading out of the underground area, facing the approaching Tīga.

With both arms occupied by the two Beloved Children, Tīga's gaze sharpened.

“Get out of the way! You'll get hurt!”

“Then take responsibility if you hurt me!”

“What kind of answer is that?!”

Tīga's eyes widened in shock at Melty's response as she blocked his path.

The distance between them continued to shrink. It seemed as though Melty would be made to pay the price for her recklessness—

“Tch! Pūka!”

“Leave those guys to me!”

At Tīga's call, Pūka leaped from his shoulder and rapidly grew larger.

Her twenty-centimeter body swelled in the blink of an eye, becoming a massive creature roughly five meters tall.

Her round tail grew proportionally larger, too. She swung it around and caught Tīga squarely in the back, sending him flying forward.

“—Tīga!”

Tīga soared through the air in a parabola, passing over Melty's head as her round eyes widened in shock.

She instinctively reached out to him, but he was too high and moving too fast for her to reach.

“See ya.”

“Tīga—!!”

Their eyes met for only an instant.

Then, from the very first step after landing, Tīga shot forward like an arrow, leaving Melty behind as she desperately shouted after him.

He didn't stop.

Detour wouldn't let her catch up to his retreating back.

“Wait! Wait, I said! Tīga! Tīgaaa!”

No matter how many times she shouted, her voice couldn't reach him.

Her outstretched hand couldn't reach him either.

The distance between them continued to widen, and eventually, even the sound of his footsteps faded away.

Behind her, Pūka's gigantic form also dissolved into particles of mana, disappearing as she pursued the retreating Tīga.

“Shit! He got away with it…”

They'd let him escape.

—That was the conclusion Subaru was forced to accept as the result of their encounter with the Beloved Children inside Kugelschreiber Castle, a battle whose final outcome had been left unresolved.


